So this approach should handle all cases efficiently. The time complexity for each type2 query is O(alpha(n)) per element processed, but each element is processed at most once across all type2 queries. So overall, the time is O(n alpha(n)) for type2 queries, which is acceptable for n up to 2e5.

The type1 and type3 queries are O(alpha(n)) per query.

