At the end, return max_len.

Wait, but wait! That would work only if the consecutive pairs have difference 1. But what about when the current element can form a valid pair with the previous, but the previous's previous might not?

Wait, no. Because the DP approach here is tracking contiguous subarrays. So if the current element and the previous have a difference of 1, then the current subarray ending at i is current_length +1. Because the subarray from i - current_length to i would all have consecutive differences of 1.

