But wait, what about when A is 1? Because if A is 1, then any Xi that is 1 would have gcd 1. But according to the problem statement, the numbers can be 1. For example, if Max's number is 1, then all Xi's that are 1 can't be friends, since gcd(1,1) is 1. So in that case, Max can't make any friends. So the code should handle that correctly.

Yes, because math.gcd(1, x) is 1 if x is 1, else 1. So for A=1, all Xi's will have gcd 1 with A, except possibly if Xi is 0? But according to the input constraints, Xi >=1. So if A is 1, the answer is 0.

