Let's recall the Lagrange interpolation formula. The Lagrange basis polynomial L_i(x) is the product for all j ≠ i of (x - j)/(i - j). Then, the interpolating polynomial is sum_{i=0 to p-1} a_i * L_i(x). 

But since we are working modulo p, division is multiplication by the modular inverse. So, for each i, we need to compute L_i(x), evaluate it to get the coefficients of x^k, multiply by a_i, then sum all these coefficients modulo p. 

