So the code should work.

Now, let's code this in Python.

Read p, then a list of integers.

Initialize total_coeffs as [0]*p.

Loop over each i from 0 to p-1:

   if a[i] is 0: skip.

   else:

      if i ==0:

          total_coeffs[0] +=1

          total_coeffs[-1] += (p-1)

          # mod p after all additions.

      else:

          for k in 1 to p-1:

              exponent = (p-1) -k

              val = pow(i, exponent, p)

              total_coeffs[k] += (-val) % p

              total_coeffs[k] %=p

After processing all i, mod all coefficients by p.

Finally, print the coefficients.

But in code, after adding each contribution, we can take mod p to prevent overflow.

So the code:

p = int(input())
a = list(map(int, input().split()))
coeff = [0] * p

for i in range(p):
    if a[i] == 0:
        continue
    if i == 0:
        # Handle i=0 case
        coeff[0] = (coeff[0] + 1) % p
        coeff[-1] = (coeff[-1] + (p - 1)) % p
    else:
        for k in range(1, p):
            exponent = (p - 1) - k
            val = pow(i, exponent, p)
            contribution = (-val) % p
            coeff[k] = (coeff[k] + contribution) % p

print(' '.join(map(str, coeff)))
