If next cell is empty: move into it (position changes), direction preserved.

If next cell has bricks: break them (cell becomes empty), and change direction.

If next cell has a concrete wall: change direction.

So in the case of a brick or concrete wall, Joe does not move into the cell. He stays in his current position, and changes direction. Only when the next cell is empty does he move into it.

So for example, if Joe is at position x, direction right. Next cell is '+', he breaks it (cell x+1 becomes '.'), changes direction to left. His new position is x, direction left. The next step would be to check below again.

So this changes the movement dynamics. Because when a brick is hit, Joe stays in place and changes direction. So the only way to move left/right is when the next cell is empty.

This is a key point. So breaking a brick or hitting a wall does not cause movement. Only direction change.

