4. Compute the number of connected components in S_x's DSU. Let this be C_S.

5. The total connected components for x's graph is C_S + (n - |S_x|).

Because the nodes not in S_x are each in their own component.

This way, we don't need to initialize a DSU with all n nodes. Only the nodes involved in x's edges.

This reduces the DSU initialization cost for each x to O(|S_x|) time, which is manageable if |S_x| is small on average.

