So the problem reduces to, for each d, check all residue groups. For each group, collect the set of characters (V, K, ?) in that group, and check that in the group, there's no both V and K. Because if a group has both, then that group cannot be assigned a single character. If all groups are okay (i.e., each group's characters are either all V and/or ?, or all K and/or ?, but not a mix of V and K), then d is possible.

