So how to compute this:

We can use dynamic programming. For each group in the sorted group order, we compute the maximum length of a sequence ending with that group.

For example:

sorted_group_order = [G1, G2, ..., Gk]

For each i from 0 to k-1:

dp[i] = 1 (can form a sequence of length 1 with just Gi)

For j from 0 to i-1:

if first_occurrence[Gi] > last_occurrence[Gj], then dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)

The maximum dp[i] is the maximum length.

But this approach would be O(k^2), which is not feasible for large k (up to 3e5 per query).

