def bfs(start_x, start_y, end_x, end_y, vertical, horizontal):
    from collections import deque
    visited = set()
    q = deque()
    q.append( (start_x, start_y, 0) )
    visited.add( (start_x, start_y) )
    while q:
        x, y, dist = q.popleft()
        if x == end_x and y == end_y:
            return dist
        # Check all four directions
        # East
        if (x+1, y) not in vertical and (x+1, y, x+1, y) not in vertical:
            if (x+1, y) not in vertical:
                nx = x + 1
                ny = y
                if 0 <= nx < W and 0 <= ny < H and (nx, ny) not in visited:
                    visited.add( (nx, ny) )
                    q.append( (nx, ny, dist+1) )
        # West
        if (x, y) not in vertical:
            nx = x -1
            ny = y
            if 0 <= nx < W and 0 <= ny < H and (nx, ny) not in visited:
                visited.add( (nx, ny) )
                q.append( (nx, ny, dist+1) )
        # North
        if (x, y) not in horizontal:
            nx = x
            ny = y +1
            if 0 <= nx < W and 0 <= ny < H and (nx, ny) not in visited:
                visited.add( (nx, ny) )
                q.append( (nx, ny, dist+1) )
        # South
        if (x, y-1) not in horizontal:
            nx = x
            ny = y -1
            if 0 <= nx < W and 0 <= ny < H and (nx, ny) not in visited:
                visited.add( (nx, ny) )
                q.append( (nx, ny, dist+1) )
    return -1  # unreachable

Wait, but the room coordinates are (x, y) where x ranges from 0 to W-1 and y from 0 to H-1. Because the dungeon has W rooms in width and H in height.

So in the BFS, we need to check if the next room (nx, ny) is within 0 <= nx < W and 0 <= ny < H.

The entrance is at (ix, iy), which is the southwest corner of the room. So the room is (ix, iy). So the code must ensure that ix and iy are within 0 <= ix < W and 0 <= iy < H. Similarly for exit.

So in the BFS, the start is (ix, iy) and the end is (ox, oy).

