A's subsequence can be taken as the first two 0s. B's subsequence is 0 (from position 0) and 1 (position 2). But the merged string is 001, which has B as a subsequence. But in this case, the output in the example was 010. But both 001 and 010 are valid, as both contain A and B as subsequences.

