Oh, right! Because the largest possible minimum for any k planks is achieved by taking the k largest planks. Because if you take any other set of k planks, the minimum of that set will be less than or equal to the k-th largest plank. So by sorting the array in non-increasing order, and for each k, compute the min between k and the k-th element (since the first k elements are the largest, their minimum is the smallest among them, which is the k-th element in the sorted list), then the maximum of these min(k, a_sorted[k-1]) is the answer.

