Well, two hexagons (x, y) and (a, b) are adjacent. The possible positions that are adjacent to both are the intersection of their neighbors. Since (x, y) and (a, b) are adjacent, their common neighbors are two positions. For example, consider (0,0) and (1,0). Their common neighbors are (0,1) and (1,-1). So, the head could move to either of those positions.

