For a middle section, the new position must be adjacent to the previous and next sections. Since the previous and next are adjacent (as per the body structure), their common neighbors are two positions. But the current position of the middle section is one of them (the one that forms the straight line), so the other possible position is the other common neighbor. So, the middle section can only move to that one position.

