The initial heap has all dishes with a_i>0, ordered by cost and index. The first customer orders 6 dishes of type 1 (0-based 0). a[0] is 6. Take 6 dishes. a[0] becomes 0. Push nothing. remaining is 0. Total is 6*6=36.

The second customer orders type 2 (0-based 1). a[1] is 6. Take 6 dishes. a[1]=0. Total is 6*66=396.

And so on. Each customer takes all their ordered dishes from their type. The last customer orders 66 dishes from type 6 (0-based 5). a[5] is 6. Take 6. remaining is 60. The heap is empty (all other dishes are 0). So total is 0.

So the code outputs 0.

This matches the sample.

The code seems correct.

Another edge case: when a customer's order can't be fulfilled. Like, when after taking some dishes, the remaining can't be fulfilled.

