But wait, the problem says that when Sereja participates in a Div2 round, he also remembers the Div1 round if it was simultaneous. So, in a type 1 entry (like 1 num2 num1), the known identifiers are num2 and num1. For type 2 entries (like 2 num), the known is just num.

So, all the identifiers that are known are stored in a set. Then, all possible Div2 rounds less than x that are not in this set, and are not part of a simultaneous pair (either as Div2 or Div1) in the known set.

But the unknown identifiers (those less than x not in the known set) can be arranged in two ways to minimize or maximize the count of missed Div2 rounds.

The minimum number of missed Div2 rounds is achieved when as many as possible of the unknown identifiers are part of simultaneous rounds. Each such pair (Div2 and Div1) would only count as one Div2 round (the Div2 one) but the Div1 is not a Div2 round. Wait, but in a simultaneous pair, the Div2 is one round. So, for each pair, the Div2 is the one Sereja could have participated in. So, the other identifiers (Div1) are not Div2 rounds, so they don't count towards the missed rounds.

But the problem is about counting Div2 rounds that Sereja missed. So, the missed rounds are all Div2 rounds that are not in the known set, and that exist between 1 and x-1 (since the current x is the one he's in now).

