But wait, t can't exceed n or k. So the maximum t is min(k, n). But if n is larger than k, then the maximum t is k. Otherwise, it's n.

So the formula becomes:

E[x^k] = sum_{t=1 to min(k, n)} (n choose t) * S(k, t) * t! * p^t

But p is 1/m here.

