So how to represent this line uniquely. For example, two points (x1,y1) and (x2,y2) are colinear with (x0,y0) if the vectors (x1 - x0, y1 - y0) and (x2 -x0, y2 - y0) are scalar multiples. So, the direction vector must be the same when simplified. 

So, for each stormtrooper, compute the direction vector (dx, dy) from (x0,y0) to (xi,yi). Then, we can represent this direction as a reduced fraction (dx/gcd, dy/gcd), where gcd is the greatest common divisor of dx and dy. But we also need to handle the sign. For example, (2,4) and (-1,-2) are scalar multiples (same line direction). So, to avoid considering these as different, we can normalize the direction vector by dividing by their greatest common divisor and ensuring that the signs are consistent. 

