So how to compute L, R, T, B for each cell?

Let's think for a cell (i,j):

L is the number of contiguous ^ to the left of (i,j) in the same row. So in row i, starting from j-1, move left until you hit a non-^ or the edge. The count is the number of consecutive ^ before j in that row.

